# 3. Agenda: Confirmed Layout and Behavior

Agenda is a shared, organization-scoped, persistent current-state agenda/blackboard. It should use the simple, familiar spreadsheet-style layout discussed for this feature, rather than a complicated dashboard or a generic blank notepad. It is not a monthly worksheet.

Display **Last Updated** at the top. It must show the date/time of the last successful Supabase save and must not advance merely because the user typed or a save was attempted. The display must reflect persisted state after the page is reopened or refreshed.

The five sections must appear in this order:

## 3.1 Wins

- Two columns.
- Twelve rows by default.
- Users can add rows.
- The exact business column headings are not established in this checkpoint. Use the existing agreed source/reference if available; do not invent headings.

## 3.2 Announcements

- Persistent, freely editable text/whiteboard area.
- Content must be saved and restored with the rest of the Agenda.

## 3.3 Rocks

Columns:

- Rocks
- Target
- Current
- Date

Users can add rows.

## 3.4 Where I Need Help

Columns:

- Name
- Where I Need Help
- Remarks

Users can add rows.

## 3.5 Items Carried Over from Last Week

Columns:

- Item
- Remarks

Users can add rows.

## 3.6 Agenda Persistence Rules

- Persist all five sections, row content, added rows, and announcement text in Supabase.
- Scope all data to the owning Organization.
- Authorized users must see the shared latest state across refreshes, revisits, and sign-ins.
- No month selector, monthly snapshots, monthly history, or copy-forward. This is a deliberate correction to the earlier October 8 discussion that had described a monthly Agenda; the later October 14 decision supersedes that earlier proposal.
- Update Last Updated only after a successful save.
- Apply CascadEffects visual tokens: navy `#082550`, blue-gray `#B4C2D1`, light blue `#E9F4F8`, charcoal `#272D2C`, white `#FFFFFF`, and coral `#E26D5C` used sparingly.
- Brand typography direction: Roboto Black, Martel Sans, and Khula. Follow the existing CascadEffects brand guide/design-system usage rather than applying every font indiscriminately.
- Keep the layout clean and spreadsheet-like, with visible section headings, table headers, editable cells/fields, and add-row affordances where specified. Do not replace the agreed structured sections with a single generic textarea.
- Autosave is required. A save failure must not be represented as a successful save; Last Updated must remain at the last confirmed successful persisted save. Provide an appropriate visible saving/error state if the existing interaction patterns support it, without inventing a new persistence model.

