# 4. Client Performance: Confirmed Behavior

Client Performance is one Runtime tab that may contain multiple independently named tables.

- It is persistent current-state operational data.
- It has no month selector, monthly snapshots/history, or copy-forward.
- Save edits to existing records and reload the latest saved state when users return.
- Reuse the existing Custom Tables infrastructure where appropriate.
- Preserve tenant isolation and authorization boundaries.
- Do not force Recruitment's monthly data model onto Client Performance.

